+# Tasks: Windows beta adoption
+
+Issue: `1f76ff32-e688-40c2-bb01-6e1392aca45d`
+
+This is an approved-plan input only after the human gates are resolved. Every
+implementation task uses RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR and produces a local commit.
+
+## Gate 0 — human decisions
+
+- [ ] Approve setup-managed consumer `.gitattributes` mutation.
+- [ ] Approve `*.sh text eol=lf` rather than Forge-directory-only patterns.
+- [ ] Approve optional Lefthook peer alignment to `^2.1.4`.
+- [ ] Approve reuse of one existing Windows matrix case for the smoke proof.
+
+No development task starts while any item above is unanswered.
+
+## W1 Task 1 — pure attributes writer
+
+Owner: one bounded implementer. Files:
+`lib/gitattributes-wiring.js`, `test/gitattributes-wiring.test.js`.
+
+1. RED: specify missing-file creation, existing-content preservation, one
+   managed block, CRLF/LF input handling, and repeated-run idempotence.
+2. GREEN: implement the smallest synchronous pure merge API. It may read/write
+   only the target `.gitattributes`; no Git or package-manager subprocesses.
+3. REFACTOR: centralize markers/content and keep errors actionable.
+4. Verify focused tests and strict lint; commit.
+
+Acceptance: user lines are byte-preserved outside the managed block, the Forge
+block is last and unique, and a second run produces no diff.
+
+## W1 Task 2 — live setup integration
+
+Owner: one bounded implementer after Task 1. Files:
+`lib/commands/setup.js`, `test/setup-gitattributes.test.js`.
+
+1. RED: run the live setup handler in a temporary repository configured with
+   `core.autocrlf=true`; prove `.gitattributes` is absent and `sample.sh` lacks
+   the required consumer LF contract.
+2. GREEN: invoke the shared writer only on setup paths that install Forge
+   shell/hook assets. Preserve `--skills-only` side-effect behavior.
+3. REFACTOR: keep setup orchestration thin and add no second policy source.
+4. Verify `git check-attr text eol`, clean index behavior, rerun idempotence,
+   focused setup/hook tests, and strict lint; commit.
+
+Acceptance: the live behavior satisfies design criteria 1-4 and no test uses a
+global timeout increase.
+
+## W1 Task 3 — spec and quality review
+
+1. Spec review every acceptance item against the exact W1 diff.
+2. Quality review path traversal, partial write, encoding, newline, and mature
+   repository preservation risks.
+3. Fix valid findings TDD-first; rerun focused tests/lint/diff.
+4. Validate and ship W1 only after both reviews pass.
+
+## W2 Task 1 — package contract alignment
+
+Owner: one bounded implementer after W1 merges. Files: `package.json`, optional
+`bun.lock`, `test/cross-platform-install.test.js`.
+
+1. RED: assert the optional peer range and validated development range share
+   the approved Lefthook major line.
+2. GREEN: align only the optional peer contract; regenerate the lock only when
+   the package manager requires it.
+3. REFACTOR: remove no dependency and introduce no install script.
+4. Run packaging dry-run with lifecycle scripts intentionally disabled for
+   inspection, focused tests, strict lint, and diff; commit.
+
+Acceptance: consumers receive one honest optional compatibility contract, with
+no bundled platform binary claimed inside the tarball.
+
+## W2 Task 2 — adoption proof and docs
+
+Owner: one bounded implementer after W2 Task 1. Files:
+`test/lefthook-check.test.js`, `docs/guides/SETUP.md`,
+`docs/reference/TOOLCHAIN.md`.
+
+1. RED: add only missing behavioral cases for Windows binary detection and
+   package-manager remediation; do not duplicate already-green cases.
+2. GREEN: make the minimum production correction only if a new test exposes a
+   real gap; otherwise keep this task tests/docs-only.
+3. Document the setup verdict, native fallback, managed LF rule, and optional
+   reviewed renormalization command.
+4. Run the W1+W2 focused suite and one existing Windows matrix smoke case.
+5. Spec/quality review, validate, then ship W2.
+
+Acceptance: documentation matches the live command and no network-dependent test
+or separate Windows workflow is added.
+
+## Forbidden overlap
+
+Do not edit process-tree/full-suite/pre-push runner files. Failures there are
+receipts for issue `54b54219-7cbc-4262-9461-a77112a7c49b`, not scope expansion.
+Do not edit any current file in open PRs #514, #522, or #523.
